INT. STORAGE FACILITY - OFFICE - NIGHT

SERIES OF SHOTS:

-- Rain on the corrugated roof. Orange sodium light bleeding through the blinds.

-- A keypad gate. Its red light blinks, blinks, blinks.

-- THE WOMAN, 30s, soaked coat, a bolt cutter bag over her shoulder, walks the long corridor of roll-up doors. Her boots squeak on the concrete.

ON PHONE (TEXT FROM NELL): where r u

ON PHONE (TEXT FROM NELL): mum's flat is empty u said you'd be done by 9

-- The woman thumbs the screen dark. Doesnt reply.

-- Fluorescent tubes flicker overhead. One dies. Another takes over.

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - CORRIDOR C - CONTINUOUS

She stops at Unit 214. A padlock the size of her fist. She sets down the bag.

INTERCOM (V.O.)
(crackling)
Unit two fourteen is on the lease til the end of the month ma'am. Just so you know.

The woman looks up at a small speaker grille above the door.

THE WOMAN
You're still here. Its past midnight.

ODELL (V.O.)
Night manager. Odell. I do the walkthroughs whether anyone's here or not.

MONTAGE - THE LOCK

-- Bolt cutters. Jaws bite. Nothing.

-- Bolt cutters again. A SNAP. The padlock drops.

-- Rain. Rain. A drip falling from a pipe into a bucket somewhere far off.

-- The door rattles upward on its track. Cold air rolls out.

INT. UNIT 214 - CONTINUOUS

Cardboard boxes. A rocking horse under a sheet. A dressing mirror turned to face the wall. Everything neat, too neat, like someone arranged it for a visit.

She pulls a box open. Photographs. Her own face at ten years old, then at twelve, then at fourteen. Every one with the eyes scratched out.

THE WOMAN
(quiet)
Okay.

Behind her the corridor lights go out one by one, towards her. Click. Click. Click.

A TEENAGE BOY, TOBY, 17, hi-vis vest two sizes too big, stands in the open doorway holding a torch.

TOBY
Sorry! Sorry. Odell sent me. Said you might need a hand carrying.

THE WOMAN
Carrying what.

TOBY
(looking past her)
...the mirror?

She turns. The mirror is facing the room now. Nobody touched it.

TIME CUT:

INT. UNIT 214 - LATER

Boxes stacked by the door. The woman sits on the rocking horse crate, calm, scrolling.

ON PHONE (TEXT FROM NELL): hello?? Priya answer me

PRIYA
(into phone, flat)
I found it, Nell. All of it.

Toby leans on the doorframe, watching the rain.

TOBY
You want me to turn the light back on in the hall?

PRIYA
Leave it.

Rain. The drip in the bucket. The mirror, quiet.

SMASH CUT TO BLACK.
